WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.940
Immunization is key to preventing infectious diseases in children.

2.1
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:12.930
We need to determine the age limits for DPT and OPV vaccines.

3.1
00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:19.470
The Universal Immunization Programme provides a schedule for vaccinations.

4.1
00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:26.870
Vaccines must be administered within specific age limits for effective immunity.

5.1
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:36.240
Options with age limits beyond 7 years for DPT and 5 years for OPV can be eliminated.

6.1
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:43.470
DPT can be given up to 7 years and OPV up to 5 years of age.

7.1
00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:49.650
Timely vaccination is crucial for preventing infectious diseases.

8.1
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:56.740
Remember DPT 7, OPV 5 for the age limits of these vaccines.

9.1
00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:03.200
Focus on key concepts like vaccination schedules and age limits.

10.1
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:10.170
Refer to UIP guidelines for the most up, to, date vaccination schedules.

11.1
00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:17.790
Remember the age limits for DPT and OPV vaccines for effective immunity.
